 "dates": "Tuesday, September 22 – Sunday, September 27, 2009",
 "logline": "A wake for a cigarette on the Delgado roof, an argument that outlasts the night, a seminar on whether a man and a woman can be friends — and on Friday, Becca drives.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "You told Hale your brother is in prison. He asked what you send him.",
   "if": "e6_hale_danny"
  },
  {
   "text": "Becca asked if the beach cleanup was a date. You said it was both. She wrote FRIDAY? on her clipboard.",
   "if": "e6_becca==\"both\""
  },
  {
   "text": "Fr. Osei, at the grill: “Your grandmother’s Mass is Tuesday at twelve-ten. I will say it myself.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "Gina wanted to know what to call the nun. You told her: Lena.",
   "if": "e6_gina_name"
  },
  {
   "text": "At the lifeguard tower Lena said she’d decided not to notice. You told her she doesn’t have to be fine with you. “I know. That’s the problem, Jack. If I stop being fine with you, I don’t know how I’m supposed to — ”",
   "if": "e6_wes==\"fine\""
  },
  {
   "text": "On the Lagoon bench: “Are we breaking up?” “We’d have to be something first, Costigan.”"
  }
 ],
